==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[pro tempore]]

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|la|en}} phrase; ''[[pro#Latin|pro]] [[tempus#Latin|tempore]]''. The preposition ''[[pro#Latin|pro]]'' means "[[for]]" and ''[[tempore#Latin|tempore]]'' is the ablative of ''[[tempus#Latin|tempus]]'' meaning "[[time]]".

===Adverb===
{{head|en}}

# [[temporarily]]; for the time being

